## The prompt keeps growing

Every tool result and every reply is added to the prompt, and the model re-reads all of it on every
call. But a model can only read so much at once: its
<GlossaryPopover term="context-window">context window</GlossaryPopover> (Ch 8). Long before that
limit, long prompts also get slower and more expensive. So the harness has to choose what the model
sees.

Below, the agent from Ch 17 has done the same task for all six rhymes. Then you ask about the first
one. To make the problem visible we set a small budget of 1,500 tokens; the model itself can read
far more. Pick what the harness does when the conversation doesn't fit:

<ContextBudget />

## Three ways to make room

- **Drop the oldest.** Simple, and often fine. But here the first task was the one you asked about.
  With it gone, the model made up an answer: a rhyme called "Old Mother Hubbard" with 18 words.
- **Summarize.** The harness asks the model to condense the old turns into a short note, then keeps
  the note instead. The summary kept "30 words", so the answer was right. Summaries lose detail,
  though, and you can't always tell in advance which details will matter.
- **Retrieve.** The harness keeps the old turns stored outside the prompt, and when a question
  comes in, finds the ones most similar in meaning, using embeddings like the map in Ch 5, and puts
  them back.<Cite id="lewis2020" /> The cat task was the closest match to the question, so it came
  back and the model answered correctly.

This is <GlossaryPopover term="retrieval">retrieval</GlossaryPopover>, the same idea behind
assistants that search your documents: they don't read everything, they look up what seems
relevant and copy it into the prompt. Memory features work the same way: notes saved outside the
model and put back into the prompt later.

<RecapCard>

- The model only knows what's in its prompt, and the prompt has a limit.
- When it fills up, the harness drops, summarizes, or retrieves text.
- Whatever is left out is simply gone for the model, and it may fill the gap by making things up.

</RecapCard>

**Next question:** the harness puts tool results and retrieved text into the same prompt as your
